  - img: a3-consent-site
    alt: "The consent screen: it says this is the publisher's own site, links the terms, and offers monthly and annual subscriptions."
    title: Choose an offer
    see: It names the publisher's own site, links the terms, and shows the blog's two offers. Choosing one is the demo's stand-in for checkout.
    why: The License Server records the subscription and sends the blog a token covering every post in the subscription, valid for an hour.
    narrow: true
  - img: a4-blog-unlocked
    alt: "Back on the blog, the same post in full, tagged 'Unlocked with OPE'."
    title: Back on the blog, unlocked
    see: The same post in full, tagged Unlocked with OPE. The other subscriber-only posts are unlocked too.
    why: The blog checked the token and keeps it in a cookie on this browser, so every covered post opens. Stop reading on this browser forgets it.
appSteps:
  - img: b1-reader-locked
    alt: "The reader app: a library of the blog's posts on the left, with locks on subscriber-only posts, and the selected post's preview and offers on the right."
    title: Open the post in a reader app
    see: A reader app with the blog's posts in a library, subscriber-only ones locked. The selected post shows its preview and the blog's offers.
    why: The app reads the blog's ordinary feed, and learns where to get access the same way the blog's own page does.
  - img: b2-consent-app
    alt: "The License Server's consent screen for the reader app, saying 'You have: OPE Demo Blog, monthly', with Allow and Deny buttons."
    title: Allow the app, no second subscription
    see: The License Server already knows the subscription from the blog. It only asks whether to let this app use it, and warns that the app isn't reviewed.
    why: One subscription, many apps. Each app gets its own token, tied to a key that never leaves the app.
    narrow: true
  - img: b3-reader-unlocked
    alt: "The reader app after allowing: every subscriber-only post in the library now shows an open lock, and the full post is on the right."
    title: Every covered post unlocks
    see: All three subscriber-only posts flip to unlocked in the library, and the post opens in full.
    why: The token covers the whole subscription, so the app reads any post in it without asking again.
  - img: b4-reader-hood
    alt: "The reader app's 'Under the hood' panel, listing each request, including two copied-token attempts refused with 401."
    title: A copied token is useless
    see: The Under the hood panel lists every request in plain language. Its copied-token test is refused twice.
    why: Each request carries a fresh proof signed by the app's key (DPoP). A token copied from logs or a screenshot fails that check.
