{# ABOUTME: The OPE demo walkthrough: screenshots of the live v0.2 demo, subscribing on the blog and in a reader app. #}
{# ABOUTME: Links to the live demo sites and the demo's source; the specification remains authoritative. #}

{% macro step(s, n) %}
<li class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,5fr)_minmax(0,7fr)] items-start rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 ring-1 ring-zinc-900/5">
  <div class="min-w-0">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="grid h-7 w-7 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-zinc-900 text-xs font-semibold text-white font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)]">{{ n }}</span>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-900">{{ s.title }}</h3>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500">What you see</p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-700">{{ s.see }}</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500">What just happened</p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-700">{{ s.why }}</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="m-0 min-w-0">
    <img src="{{ ('/ope/demo/img/' + s.img + '.webp') | url }}" alt="{{ s.alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      class="block w-full rounded-xl ring-1 ring-zinc-900/10 bg-white {% if s.narrow %}max-w-sm mx-auto{% endif %}">
  </figure>
</li>
{% endmacro %}

<section class="py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-400/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-emerald-700 ring-1 ring-inset ring-emerald-400/20">Live demo · OPE v0.2, proposed</span>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 text-balance">Subscribe once, read on the site or in any app</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-zinc-600">A reader subscribes to a blog at its <strong class="font-semibold text-zinc-900">License Server</strong>, then reads subscriber-only posts on the blog itself and in a separate reader app, with no second subscription. The blog never handles a password or a payment. Every screenshot below is from the live demo, which implements the <a href="{{ '/ope/spec/0.2/' | url }}" class="text-emerald-700 underline">v0.2 draft</a>.</p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="{{ demo.post }}" class="rounded-full bg-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 hover:bg-emerald-400 no-underline transition-colors">Try it on the blog</a>
      <a href="{{ demo.reader }}" class="rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-600 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-900/10 hover:text-zinc-900 hover:ring-zinc-900/20 no-underline transition-colors">Open the reader app</a>
      <a href="{{ demo.repo }}" class="rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-600 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-900/10 hover:text-zinc-900 hover:ring-zinc-900/20 no-underline transition-colors">Source on GitHub</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-5 ring-1 ring-zinc-900/5">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900">The blog</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-600">The publisher. It serves posts, and checks a token before showing a subscriber-only one. A static Eleventy site with a small function in front.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-5 ring-1 ring-zinc-900/5">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900">The License Server</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-600">Signs readers in, keeps their subscriptions, and issues short-lived tokens. Usually run by someone else, the way a payment provider is.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-5 ring-1 ring-zinc-900/5">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900">A reader app</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-600">Any app the reader chooses. It gets its own token from the License Server and presents it to the blog.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pb-20" aria-labelledby="on-blog">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 id="on-blog" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">On the blog itself</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-600">The site unlocks its own posts in the browser (the draft's Web profile).</p>
    <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-6 list-none p-0">
      {% for s in blogSteps %}{{ step(s, loop.index) }}{% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pb-20" aria-labelledby="in-app">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 id="in-app" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">The same subscription, in a reader app</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-600">Continuing in the same browser, after subscribing on the blog.</p>
    <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-6 list-none p-0">
      {% for s in appSteps %}{{ step(s, loop.index + blogSteps.length) }}{% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pb-20" aria-labelledby="account">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,5fr)_minmax(0,7fr)] items-start">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <h2 id="account" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">One account, every app</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-600">At the License Server, the reader sees one subscription and every app connected to it: here, the blog itself and the reader app. Cancelling the subscription locks the posts everywhere on the next request. Disconnecting an app ends only that app's access.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="m-0 min-w-0">
      <img src="{{ '/ope/demo/img/c1-account.webp' | url }}" alt="The reader's account at the License Server: one active monthly subscription, and two connected apps, the publisher's site and OPE Reader, each with a Disconnect button." loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-xl ring-1 ring-zinc-900/10 bg-white">
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pb-20" aria-labelledby="atproto">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 ring-1 ring-zinc-900/5">
      <span class="rounded-full bg-amber-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-amber-800 ring-1 ring-inset ring-amber-900/10">Prototype</span>
      <h2 id="atproto" class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">Subscriber-only posts on atproto</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-600">atproto spaces, now in alpha, let a space hand each "may this account read?" decision to an outside service. The demo's License Server can be that service, answering from the same subscription. See the <a href="{{ '/ope/spec/0.2/' | url }}#e-atproto-profile-deferred" class="text-emerald-700 underline">Profile E notes</a> and <a href="{{ demo.atproto }}" class="text-emerald-700 underline">the demo's atproto page</a>.</p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900">Works</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-600 list-disc pl-5">
            <li>The whole path, against Bluesky's own spaces-alpha server run locally. A reader signs in with their atproto account to link it. The space asks the License Server before issuing a credential. An app reads the posts with that credential.</li>
            <li>Credentials go only to linked readers with an active subscription. Each request must be signed by the space's owner.</li>
            <li>A multi-user app syncs the space once, then shows the posts only to users with their own subscription, checked with an OPE License Token.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900">Not yet</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-600 list-disc pl-5">
            <li>A hosted space (the alpha is invite-only).</li>
            <li>Spaces in the demo's reader app.</li>
            <li>Cutting off a credential already issued: after a cancellation, it lasts until it expires (10 minutes).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pb-24" aria-labelledby="run">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 id="run" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">Run it yourself</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-600">The <a href="{{ demo.repo }}" class="text-emerald-700 underline">demo's source</a> runs locally with one command (<code>./run-demo.sh</code>), and puts both servers on a Cloudflare account with another (<code>./deploy-cloudflare.sh</code>). Adding OPE to your own Eleventy site takes four steps with <code>eleventy-plugin-ope</code>. You don't run a License Server yourself.</p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xs text-zinc-500">Screenshots captured {{ demo.captured }} from the live demo. The demo implements a proposed draft, which may change in response to <a href="{{ spec.commentsUrl }}" class="underline">comments</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
